schema: "0.4"
id: npl-blueprint-15-admin-mcp-custom-scopes
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo (structured prompt-definition language + MCP agent toolchain) — Admin: MCP Custom Scopes screen.
# Theme tenets: cool drafting sheet, faint grid texture, thin cyan rules + monospace annotations, near-square 2px corners, one warm redline for markup.
# Palette: sheet #f5f8fc, navy ink #14263f, blueprint-blue #245ea8, drafting cyan #0e9bd6, redline #c05a3e.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    platform-administration surface for NoizuPromptLingo — a structured
    prompt-definition language and MCP agent toolchain. The register is a
    technical drafting sheet: cool, exacting, calm — "drawn by someone who
    measures twice." Structure is the aesthetic — a faint background grid, thin
    cyan rules, dimension lines, and monospace callout labels do the work.
    Engineered IBM Plex Sans for UI, IBM Plex Mono for every precise value.
    Near-square corners, nearly flat surfaces, no gradients or glow. The only
    warm color is a single red-oxide redline reserved for markup and attention.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the Admin: MCP Custom Scopes screen of
    NoizuPromptLingo — a global library of reusable MCP scope presets that org
    and project admins can later apply to a project. Scope trees are the hero of
    this shot.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (three columns over a faint blueprint grid): a slim LEFT ADMIN
    NAV RAIL that reads like a sheet index (thin cyan active left-rule, small mono
    section labels); a SCOPE PRESET LIST column; and a wide PRESET EDITOR panel. A
    monospace breadcrumb path "admin / mcp-custom-scopes" and a title "Custom
    Scopes" in medium-weight sans sit at the top.

    SCOPE PRESET LIST (left column, title-block header "Presets"): a vertical list
    of global presets, each row a preset name in sans with a monospace tool-count
    and a usage count ("used by 6"). The selected preset carries a 2px
    blueprint-blue left-rule and medium weight; a small blueprint-blue "New
    preset" button pinned at the top.

    PRESET EDITOR FORM (center/right panel, title-block header "Edit preset"):
    a name field and a description field (sans) with small monospace
    dimension-labels above, then the INCLUDED TOOL / PERMISSION SET rendered as a
    SCOPE TREE — nested rows connected by thin cyan structural rules, each node a
    monospace tool/permission identifier (server.tool.action) with a checkbox
    sitting on the grid; enabled nodes marked, a couple of parent groups
    collapsed. This monospace scope tree with cyan connectors is the focal point.
    A blueprint-blue primary "Save preset" button at the bottom.

    PRESET USAGE DRAWER (floating in from the right — the one place elevation
    lifts, a minimal cool shadow, near-square corners; header "Applied by"): a
    list of orgs and projects currently applying the selected preset, each row a
    monospace project path (org/project) with a small muted role; a redline
    "editing affects 6 projects" caution at the top drawn as a left redline rule
    + faint tint with the note in ink.

    PALETTE & TYPE: a pale cool drafting-sheet canvas carrying dark navy drafting
    ink. Structure is blueprint blue; thin rules, tree connectors, and highlights
    are a drafting cyan; a single warm red-oxide redline is reserved for cautions
    and attention — the red pencil on a blue drawing. Neutrals are cool-tinted
    toward blue, never warm, never pure gray. Engineered IBM Plex Sans for UI and
    body; IBM Plex Mono carries every precise value — tool and permission
    identifiers, scope paths, project paths, counts, and the callout labels above
    fields.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: near-square corners — drawn, not soft, not stamped. Borders
    are the drawing: thin single-pixel cyan and blueprint-blue rules form every
    cell divider, tree connector, panel edge, and dimension line; surfaces are the
    paper between them. Nearly flat — the list and editor rest on a rule and a
    faint tone step, never a drop shadow; only the usage drawer lifts. The faint
    blueprint grid sits under the whole canvas, static and low-contrast.

    MOOD: precise, technical, trustworthy within five seconds. Cool, exacting,
    calm — a configuration surface drawn on an engineer's drafting table where
    correctness and legibility of structure matter more than warmth.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Admin: MCP Custom Scopes — a scope preset list with usage counts, a preset editor whose permission set is a monospace scope tree, and a preset-usage drawer"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Cool drafting sheet, faint blueprint grid, thin cyan tree connectors + rules, monospace scope identifiers, near-square corners, single warm redline for caution — not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear visual hierarchy, plausible real-product admin layout; the monospace scope tree with cyan connectors reads as the focal point"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"

tags: [npl-blueprint, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup]
